"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative focused on enhanced security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project kicked off in Q3 2023 with a meeting on July 15th. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the design phase, with a prototype for secure file sharing tested ahead of schedule. The next phases involve development (led by Omar Jensen), user interface enhancements starting in October, and a compliance plan. The project budget was initially approved at $2M, later adjusted to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses, with an additional $55,000 allocated for the compliance plan. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, are being updated for implementation next January. Feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November, and a celebration for the testing milestone is scheduled for October 10th."
